@CC ==================================================================
@CC FINGER:MODE - compile and link the PLANC Finger server (TCP port 79)
@CC Run as SYSTEM:  @MODE FINGER:MODE,,
@CC Then read FINGER:LIST for *** lines, and check that
@CC LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED printed nothing.
@CC
@CC MON-CALL-1B-A00 is needed twice over: TerminalStatus (330B) has no
@CC MONn routine, so FINGER calls it with MONITOR_CALL, and SLIB itself
@CC uses MONITOR_CALL too (without the library the link leaves 5MON_P
@CC undefined - measured). SLIBF00:DEFS must be on the pack.
@CC
@CC Libraries: ND's SLIB Programmer's Guide (ND-860372, section 2)
@CC lists SLIB, NK-100-1BANK, PLANC-UTILLIB-1B, MON-CALL-1BANK and
@CC PLANC-1BANK for a 1-bank program. NK-100-1BANK is not loaded: SLIB
@CC already contains the NK routines, and loading it only prints
@CC "Redefinition" lines. PLANC-UTILLIB-1B is not loaded: no copy of it
@CC is known to exist, and the link resolves every entry without it.
@CC
@CC The old outputs are deleted first, as ND's own COMP-TCCOM:MODE does:
@CC a quoted name below means CREATE, and the compiler and the linker
@CC both refuse with FILE ALREADY EXISTS if the file is still there. On
@CC the very first build the deletes answer NO SUCH FILE NAME; that is
@CC harmless.
@CC ==================================================================
@DELETE-FILE FINGER:LIST
@DELETE-FILE FINGER:BRF
@DELETE-FILE FINGER:PROG
@PLANC-100-F00
COMPILE FINGER:PLNC,"FINGER:LIST","FINGER"
EXIT
@BRF-LINKER-C01
PROGRAM-FILE "FINGER"
LOAD FINGER
LIBRARY-MODE ON
LOAD (TCP-IP)SLIB-NRE-1B-B01
LOAD (TCP-IP)SLIB-REE-1B-B01
LOAD MON-CALL-1B-A00
LOAD PLANC-1BANK-F00
LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED
EXIT
@CC END OF FILE
